What is `tmux` and why should you use it?

`tmux` is a terminal multiplexer — it lets you create multiple terminal sessions inside a single window and keep them running in the background.

  Why use it?
• Detach and reconnect to sessions anytime  
• Keep long-running jobs alive even after logout  
• Split your terminal into multiple panes

  How to install:

• Ubuntu/Debian: `sudo apt install tmux`  
• CentOS/RHEL: `sudo yum install tmux`  

  Essential commands:

• `tmux new -s mysession` – start a new session  
• `Ctrl-b d` – detach the session  
• `tmux list-sessions` – view running sessions  
• `tmux attach -t mysession` – reconnect

